# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Orbit — Single Sign-On (Google OAuth) credentials
#
# Copy the vars you need into your main .env to switch Orbit's "Sign in with
# Google" button from a clear "not configured" message to a real Google
# OAuth 2.0 sign-in flow.
#
# Behaviour:
#   • BOTH GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID + GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET set → SSO enabled.
#   • Either missing → /api/auth/sso/google redirects straight back to
#     /login?sso=unconfigured (dev/demo safe — the app never breaks).
#
# See lib/sso.ts (SSO_SETUP_DOC) for the full walkthrough.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OAuth 2.0 Client ID from Google Cloud Console.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# OAuth 2.0 Client Secret — server-only, NEVER expose to the browser.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret

# ── Where to get credentials ──
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# 2. Create (or pick) a project → "Create Credentials" → "OAuth client ID"
#    → Application type: "Web application".
# 3. Under "Authorized redirect URIs" add exactly:
#      <your-app-origin>/api/auth/sso/google/callback
#    e.g. http://localhost:3000/api/auth/sso/google/callback for local dev.
# 4. Copy the generated Client ID + Client Secret above.
#
# Production note: this scaffold matches SSO logins to EXISTING users by
# email only (no JIT auto-provisioning) and uses a placeholder OAuth "state"
# value. A real deployment should add CSRF state verification (random nonce,
# stashed + checked on callback) — see lib/sso.ts for exactly where.
